================================================================================
Evaluation data: parallel/ (fetched, not redistributed)
================================================================================

The configs under configs/ and the `--use-sample-data` demo name files under
parallel/. Those files are not in this repository. `scripts/fetch_flores.py`
downloads them from the FLORES+ dataset, and a run aborts naming that script if
they are absent.

  Dataset:  FLORES+ (Open Language Data Initiative)
  Source:   https://huggingface.co/datasets/openlanguagedata/flores_plus
  License:  CC-BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)

A copy fetched that way is under CC-BY-SA 4.0, so redistributing it carries the
same license and requires attribution. FLORES+ is intended for evaluation, not
as training data, and asks users to cite the original FLORES papers, in
particular:

  NLLB Team et al. "Scaling neural machine translation to 200 languages."
  Nature 630 (2024).

Six of the shipped language codes name a FLORES+ configuration whose code
differs from the filename: cmn_Hani holds cmn_Hans, fas_Arab holds pes_Arab,
mni_Mtei holds mni_Beng, and the fetch script resolves each from the dataset's
own iso_639_3 and iso_15924 fields.

================================================================================
Third-party tokenizers referenced in examples
================================================================================

Example configurations may reference tokenizers from the Hugging Face Hub or
from tiktoken. Those tokenizers are downloaded at run time from their
respective sources and are not redistributed in this repository. The bundled
sample tokenizers (tokenizers/bpe.json, tokenizers/unigramlm.json) are small
BPE and Unigram tokenizers included only to run the demo.
